      "content": "Even if you think you are up to date on your vaccinations, a deep puncture wound from a rusty object requires professional evaluation to check your tetanus status. While Neosporin and peroxide can clean superficial wounds, they may not be sufficient to prevent serious infection from deep, contaminated injuries. For your safety, please have a healthcare provider look at the wound to rule out deep tissue damage or necessary antibiotics.",
