      "content": "Attempting to manage a deep puncture wound from a rusty object solely with home remedies carries a significant risk of serious infection, even if you clean it thoroughly. Hydrogen peroxide can damage healthy tissue, and while Neosporin helps protect the surface, it doesn't address deeper contamination or infection risk. For peace of mind and safety, please call your primary care physician or an urgent care line for advice on the best, most affordable next step.",
